{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpktCpsjfHdJnhZGss4w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Cloudflare docs don't say `wrangler versions secret bulk` can delete secrets. They describe it only as \"Create or update a secret variable for a Worker.\" To delete a secret and create a new Worker version, use `wrangler versions secret delete <KEY>`.\n\nYou can delete in bulk with the top-level `wrangler secret bulk` command, though. In a JSON file, set the key to `null`, for example `{\"OLD_SECRET\": null}`, then run `wrangler secret bulk secrets.json`. This needs Wrangler 4.97.0 or later and doesn't work with `.env`/`.dev.vars` files. Unlike the `versions` commands, `secret bulk` deploys the change right away.\n\nSources:\n- [Wrangler Workers commands](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/commands/workers/)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":471,"cache_read_input_tokens":4552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":471},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98ca052b-c609-4020-bf42-c03073586cbc","uuid":"230b7b72-8b8c-4977-a69c-8bf7d39464ce","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:18:53.483Z","request_id":"req_011CfpktCZ1XZkespMsiaufr"}
